# Favalog environment variables (example).
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values. `.env.local` is
# git-ignored and must NEVER be committed. This example contains variable NAMES
# ONLY — no real secrets.
#
# The existing frontend runs entirely on mock data and does NOT require any of
# these to build or run. They become relevant only once the Supabase backend is
# wired into the app in a later task.

# --- Public Supabase configuration (safe to expose to the browser) ----------
# Only NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables are ever sent to the client. For local development
# these come from `npx supabase status` after `npm run supabase:start`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# Supabase's current key terminology: the *publishable* key (formerly "anon").
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Server-only secret (NEVER exposed to the browser) ----------------------
# The secret (service-role) key bypasses Row Level Security and is intended for
# trusted server-side administrative processes only (e.g. future catalog
# ingestion). It is NOT required for normal application startup. Do not prefix
# it with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never read it from client code.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=
